---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import photo from '../assets/me.jpg';
---

<section id="about" class="bg-blush">
  <div class="wrapper flex flex-col py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 class="mt-0 mb-6 font-grotesque text-4xl font-bold text-accent">About</h2>
    <div class="prose prose-lg lg:prose-xl">
      <div class="float-left -mt-1 rounded-2xl py-0 pr-6">
        <Image
          src={photo}
          alt="Armando Sosa"
          width={240}
          densities={[1, 2]}
          format="webp"
          quality={80}
          class="w-60 rounded-2xl"
        />
      </div>
      <p>
        Hello! My full name is <em>Armando Quetzalcoatl Sosa Garay</em>, but my friends just call me
        <strong> Armando</strong>. All three of them.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've been a remote frontend engineer since 2009, working with companies in New York, San
        Francisco, and Colombia. I'm currently <strong
          >Tech Lead at <a href="https://jiveworld.com">Jiveworld</a></strong
        >, where I've spent the last eight years architecting the frontend platform — including
        custom rendering technology, AI-powered localization tooling, and the design system it all
        runs on.
      </p>

      <p>
        Before programming, I was a graphic designer — fun fact: that's one of the worst-paid
        professions in Mexico, which is a big part of why I pivoted. I'm a small Mexican dude who's
        been doing internet stuff for what feels like an eternity, and outside of work you'll
        usually find me at church, playing music, or hanging out with my wonderful wife.
      </p>

      <p>
        Eating is basically a competitive sport for me at this point, and honestly, it's not my
        fault I live in the country with the best food in the <del>world</del> universe.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you want to know more, you can <strong
          ><a href="https://twitter.com/soska">follow me on Twitter</a></strong
        > or send me an electronic letter to <em>arm.sosa[at]gmail.com</em>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
